From: PowOS <noreply@powback.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kdecoration: configurable resize zones around windows (touch screens)

Windeco/ExtendedResizeBorders (breezerc, logical pixels, default 0 = as before): invisible resize-only borders that
wide around every window - sides, bottom and top, so all four corners resize - beyond its visible borders, except
along an edge a maximized window fills. On a touch screen a finger can't hit a 1 px border; PowOS's phone build sets
it (/etc/xdg/breezerc).
---
--- a/kdecoration/breezedecoration.cpp
+++ b/kdecoration/breezedecoration.cpp
@@ -433,7 +433,21 @@
         extSides = extSize;
     }
 
-    setResizeOnlyBorders(QMarginsF(extSides, 0, extSides, extBottom));
+    // A configured size (touch screens: a finger can't hit a 1 px border): around every window, beyond its borders,
+    // the top too, so all four corners resize.
+    qreal extTop = 0;
+    if (const int configured = m_internalSettings->extendedResizeBorders(); configured > 0) {
+        const qreal size = KDecoration3::snapToPixelGrid(configured, window()->nextScale());
+        if (!isMaximizedHorizontally()) {
+            extSides = std::max(extSides, size);
+        }
+        if (!isMaximizedVertically()) {
+            extBottom = std::max(extBottom, size);
+            extTop = size;
+        }
+    }
+
+    setResizeOnlyBorders(QMarginsF(extSides, extTop, extSides, extBottom));
 
     qreal topLeftRightRadius = 0;
     qreal bottomLeftRadius = 0;
--- a/kdecoration/breezesettingsdata.kcfg
+++ b/kdecoration/breezesettingsdata.kcfg
@@ -104,6 +104,13 @@
        <default>false</default>
     </entry>
 
+    <!-- invisible resize zones around every window, logical pixels (touch screens); 0: only where there are no borders -->
+    <entry name="ExtendedResizeBorders" type = "Int">
+       <default>0</default>
+       <min>0</min>
+       <max>64</max>
+    </entry>
+
     <!-- window specific settings -->
     <entry name="ExceptionType" type="Enum">
       <choices>
